# Mad Libs Email Patterns

## The Philosophy

"Personalization isn't writing 20 different email sequences. It's writing ONE email and swapping out micro-sections: the testimonial shown matches their industry, the CTA matches their product stage, the example matches their tech stack. Most of the email is identical — you just swap the 2-3 sentences that create relevance."

## Pattern 1: Conditional Content Block

```liquid
{% if subscriber.primary_challenge == "audience" %}
Your focus on audience growth is exactly why I created this guide.
Over the next few weeks, I'll be sharing strategies that have
helped creators like you double their subscriber count.
{% elsif subscriber.primary_challenge == "sales" %}
Converting subscribers to customers is both art and science.
I'll be sharing the exact framework that generated $650K in
attributed revenue for one of my clients.
{% elsif subscriber.primary_challenge == "automation" %}
Getting off the email hamster wheel means building systems.
I'll show you how to set it up once and let it run for months.
{% else %}
No matter where you are in your email marketing journey,
I've got something valuable for you.
{% endif %}
```

**The fallback is always the generic version you probably already have.** Personalization is additive.

## Pattern 2: Identity-Aware Language Swaps

Use glossary automation fields for natural language variation:

```liquid
As a {{ subscriber.ident_singular }}, I know how challenging it is
to {{ subscriber.primary_challenge_description }}.
```

This produces: "As a freelance designer, I know how challenging it is to find clients who value quality design work."

Or for case studies:
```liquid
{% case subscriber.business_type %}
  {% when "agency" %}
    Take Sarah, who runs a 12-person design agency in Portland.
    She was spending 20 hours a week on manual email campaigns...
  {% when "freelancer" %}
    Take Marcus, a freelance developer in Austin.
    He was losing 3 out of every 4 proposals he sent...
  {% when "saas" %}
    Take DataPulse, a SaaS company with 2,000 users.
    Their trial-to-paid conversion was stuck at 3%...
{% endcase %}
```

## Pattern 3: Dynamic PS (Offer Funnel CTA)

Put this in your email TEMPLATE, not individual emails:

```liquid
{% capture ps_raw %}
{% if subscriber.next_offer == "basic_course" %}
PS — Ready to level up? [The Fundamentals Course](link) is the best place to start. Helped {{ subscriber.ident_plural }} just like you get their first wins.
{% elsif subscriber.next_offer == "premium_course" %}
PS — Loved the basics? [Go deeper with the Premium Course](link). Includes advanced automation blueprints.
{% elsif subscriber.next_offer == "coaching" %}
PS — Want hands-on help? [Book a coaching session](link). We'll build your automation system together.
{% endif %}
{% endcapture %}
{% assign ps = ps_raw | strip %}

{% if ps != blank %}
—
{{ ps }}
{% endif %}
```

### Random variation (rotate between 2 descriptions per product):

```liquid
{% assign rand = "now" | date: "%s" | modulo: 2 %}
{% if subscriber.next_offer == "basic_course" %}
  {% if rand == 0 %}
    {% capture pitch %}Pitch variation A{% endcapture %}
  {% else %}
    {% capture pitch %}Pitch variation B{% endcapture %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
```

### Override for seasonal promotions:

```liquid
{% capture override %}{% endcapture %}  {# Empty = no override #}
{# Uncomment to override: {% capture override %}🎉 Black Friday: 40% off everything through Monday!{% endcapture %} #}

{% if override != blank %}
  {% capture ps_raw %}{{ override }}{% endcapture %}
{% else %}
  {# Normal offer funnel PS logic here #}
{% endif %}
```

## Pattern 4: Sales Sequence Pivots

Clone the key sales email per primary challenge. Keep 80% identical, change the opening paragraph and the angle:

**For "audience growth" segment:**
> You told me you're focused on growing your audience. So let me ask: what if you could double your opt-in rate without spending a dime on ads?

**For "sales" segment:**
> You mentioned sales is your top priority. Here's the thing most creators miss: you probably already have enough subscribers to hit your revenue goals. You just need a better system for pitching them.

**For unsegmented (fallback):**
> Whether you're focused on growth, sales, or automation, there's one thing that changes everything: understanding who's on your list and what they actually want from you.

## Pattern 5: Content Snippet Reuse

Kit content snippets for frequently-used personalized blocks:

Create snippet `offer_cta`:
```
{% case subscriber.next_offer %}
  {% when "basic_course" %}
    → [Check out The Fundamentals](link)
  {% when "premium_course" %}
    → [Go deeper with Premium](link)
{% endcase %}
```

Then use `{{ snippet.offer_cta }}` wherever needed. (Note: inline content snippets require the `###` split workaround — see liquid-templating.md)

## Fallback Strategy

### Option 1: Catchall OR copy
Use the "or" language: "Whether you're looking to start, grow, or scale your business..."

This is what you probably already have. It becomes the `else` block in your conditionals.

### Option 2: Default to majority segment
If 45% of people say "audience growth" → default to audience growth language for unsegmented subscribers.

**Caveat from Brennan**: Safe for soft personalization (swap a testimonial). Risky for hard personalization (calling them a "marketer" when they might be a developer).

### Option 3: Prompt them to segment
For the unsegmented 15-20%, include a "complete your survey" CTA instead of personalized content.

## Scope: What to Personalize (Start Small)

| Priority | Element | Effort | Impact |
|----------|---------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Welcome Email 1 | Low | Highest |
| 2 | Newsletter PS (via template) | Set once | Ongoing |
| 3 | Key sales email (1 of 5) | Medium | High |
| 4 | Subject lines (identity callout) | Low | Medium |
| 5 | Sales page headline | Medium | High |
| 6 | Full sales sequence (all emails) | High | Highest |

Start with #1 and #2. Add others over time.

## Justin Welsh Results

- 6 emails personalized on business_type + business_stage
- 5-6 hours of extra writing
- 38% higher purchase rate vs control
- ~$650K attributed revenue on $1.6M launch
- Key: personalized the "Why YOU Need This" email + micro-sections in others
